Wait for left index: getMacroBlock(tx-1, ty) -> currentMacroBlockRow[(tx-1)+1] = current[tx]. Yes.

For above: getMacroBlock(tx, ty-1) -> previousMacroBlockRow[tx+1]. Yes.
Above-left: previous[tx]. Yes.

But if left is null and we set current[tx]? We fill with filler so not null. Fine.

For tx=0, above-left is previous[0], which might equal left? No; above-left at (x-1,y-1) = (-1,ty-1), not needed. We can pass null and it remains filler.

